  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Education for Children from the Plateau, Eastern DRC</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Many children living in the war-affected plateau area of the Democratic Republic of Congo do not have the opportunity to go to schools with proper facilities, reading materials or even exercise books.  School buildings are ramshackle.  Teachers have rarely been adequately trained and often go for long periods without even being paid.  The project will work in this neglected and isolated region by training teachers to improve their teaching methods.  They will distribute school kits with essential educational material such as books and pens. And they will also work with parents and communities using theatre, drama and songs to encourage them to send their children to school and to value education. As a result thousands more children will enrol and stay in school, they will get better marks in their exams and have more confidence in their ability to learn.</narrative>
  </description>
